# {{title}}

Quarto report: `report.qmd` renders to PDF (TinyTeX) and Word.

- Render: `quarto render report.qmd` (or `--to pdf` / `--to docx`). Rendered files are git-ignored.
- Write Pandoc/Quarto Markdown; it is linted (not reformatted) after each edit. Fix what markdownlint and typos report.
- Figures: put files in `figures/`, include as `![Caption](figures/x.png){#fig-x}`, reference as `@fig-x`.
- Citations: cite only keys that exist in the bibliography named in the front matter; if a source is missing, ask the user to add it in Zotero. Never invent references.
- No Python here by default. If the report needs computed results, ask whether to convert it to a `new-project data` project.
- VS Code profile: {{profile}}, in `.vscode/profile`. If the work changes (e.g. notebooks arrive), switch with `vsc --set <profile>` (`vsc --list` shows them); never open VS Code windows unless asked.
